 "text": "Hi, how you doing right now? For a small wedding of a few hundred people, yes. For a large wedding or one with big venue fees, it can easily eat up most of the receipts. Then a planner can really help with everything from guest lists to venue bookings. It frees up your time to rest. Mostly it means the wedding morning, with the ceremony, Then breakfast and photos. Some plans include the reception venue in that day too. It is if you booked venue that's booked out for months. That's often the hardest person to please. A small family wedding with a dine out menu can still feel very special.",
